From the user input, and using the guide below, you will implement client-side
authentication features using Better Auth.

# Hands on guide

This project uses [Better Auth](https://www.better-auth.com/) for
authentication. For server-side patterns, see [Auth
Server](mdc:.cursor/rules/auth-server.mdc).

## The `useAuth()` Composable

The `useAuth()` composable provides all auth functionality on the client:

```ts
const {
  user, // Computed<User | null> - current user
  session, // Computed<Session | null> - current session
  loggedIn, // Computed<boolean> - is user logged in
  client, // Better Auth client - for advanced operations
  signIn, // Sign in methods
  signUp, // Sign up methods
  signOut, // Sign out function
  fetchSession, // Refresh session data
  apiKey, // API key management
} = useAuth();
```

## Sign In with Email/Password

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
const { client: auth } = useAuth();

async function handleSignIn(email: string, password: string) {
  const { data, error } = await auth.signIn.email({
    email,
    password,
    callbackURL: "/dash", // redirect after sign in
  });
  if (error) throw createError(error);
  // do something, usually a reload
  // example: await reloadNuxtApp({ path: '/dash' })
}
</script>
```

## Sign Up

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
const { client: auth } = useAuth();

async function handleSignUp(email: string, password: string) {
  const { error } = await auth.signUp.email({
    name: email,
    email,
    password,
    callbackURL: "/dash",
  });
  if (error) throw createError(error);
  await reloadNuxtApp({ path: "/dash" });
}
</script>
```

## Sign In with Magic Link

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
const { client: auth } = useAuth();
const toast = useToast();

